        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Ace Driver made extensive use of the CPU Assist technique whereby a trailing player would be given a significant speed boost to allow them to catch the leading player. However, the speed boost continued for a short while after the losing player had overtaken the leader - leading to a tactic known as boosting where a player would deliberately allow themselves to lose the lead, then during the last half of the last game lap would easily take back the lead with no hope of the opposing player catching them.\n\nBoosting also meant that straight skill races were difficult to have as CPU assist would be continually changing the losing players speed and position.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Ace Driver hacía un uso extensivo de la técnica CPU Assist, con la que un jugador que iba detrás recibía un impulso de velocidad considerable para poder alcanzar al líder. Sin embargo, ese impulso continuaba durante un breve tiempo después de que el jugador rezagado hubiera superado al líder. Esto dio lugar a una táctica conocida como \"boosting\", en la que un jugador se dejaba adelantar deliberadamente y, durante la última mitad de la última vuelta, recuperaba la ventaja con facilidad, sin que el rival tuviera posibilidad de alcanzarlo.\n\nEl boosting también dificultaba las carreras de pura habilidad, porque el CPU Assist cambiaba continuamente la velocidad y la posición del jugador que iba perdiendo.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1994",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
